      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "apps/cli · client process\nClient\ntransport · controller\nstartup · output capture",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "apps/cli · daemon process\nDaemon\nspool · supervisor · lifetime\nlogger · worker ↗",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "01\nSTATED\n↗\nMake policy a required input.\n\nThe existing daemon-package snapshot replaces CLI defaults and optional thresholds. The mechanisms still live in apps/cli.",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "02\nSTATED\n↗\nChoose the clock by client purpose.\n\nStatus observation uses 100 ms; ordinary one-response calls use 250 ms. Execute admission has 5 s; accepted completion has no deadline.",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "03\nSTATED\n↗\nKeep two recovery allowances.\n\nAn authenticated accepted close can reattach execute. A known manifest can resume fetch. Defaults remain one each, with a fresh fetch allowance per execute attempt.",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "04\nSTATED\n↗\nUse one set of byte limits end to end.\n\nCapture, spool, worker checks and transfer codec consume output policy; control framing has its own limits. Small results stay inline, larger ones spill.",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "05\nSTATED\n↗\nSample memory from the same snapshot.\n\nResource derivation leaves the CLI. RSS hysteresis, worker heap, sampling cadence and the replacement circuit use required resource values.",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "06\nSTATED\n↗\nRoute the quieter clocks and caps too.\n\nStartup retries and ownership, stop, idle, drain acknowledgements, logs and traces all take policy. An unused startup-timeout option disappears. Intentional missing deadlines stay missing.",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "07\nSTATED\n↗\nMove small test knobs into adapters.\n\nSeven new helpers translate legacy test inputs into validated policies. Runtime compatibility overloads disappear; new tests exercise custom values and preserved recovery. Users get no tuning knobs.",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "08\nUNEXPLAINED\n↗\nA later completion can change the reported error.\n\nAfter reattachment accepts, a malformed completion escapes as corrupt in the head. The base returns the earlier closed error. The PR does not request this difference.",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "09\nUNEXPLAINED\n↗\nA numeric fetch allowance is not a fetch loop.\n\nOn clean EOF during result-fetch, the head fails after one fetch even with its resume allowance set to two. The new count does not grant another fetch on that path.",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "10\nUNEXPLAINED\n↗\nSome test inputs and assertions change scope.\n\nLocal derivation cases are deleted. Spill fixtures and expected thresholds change; a transport adapter raises inline=0 to 64 KiB, so some cleanup cases no longer force disk storage.",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "11\nUNEXPLAINED\n↗\nEnforce retirement with source-string bans.\n\nThe package meta-test adds retired constant names and optional-input spellings to a production-source exclusion list.",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
